WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.469
Driver Quick Start covers the complete mobile stop flow.

2
00:00:06.469 --> 00:00:12.938
Use only your assigned work identity and route.

3
00:00:12.938 --> 00:00:19.406
Before leaving, open the Driver workspace, confirm the vehicle, review the stop order, and read addresses, appointment times, access notes, and special instructions.

4
00:00:19.406 --> 00:00:25.875
Contact Dispatch immediately if the route or vehicle does not match your assignment.

5
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:31.281
Start the route only when the vehicle is loaded and ready to leave.

6
00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:36.688
At each destination, review the stop before entering the property.

7
00:00:36.688 --> 00:00:42.094
Record arrival when you are physically at the stop.

8
00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:47.500
Arrival is an operational timestamp, so do not tap it early from another location simply to move the screen forward.

9
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:55.358
Complete the service and capture every required proof item before departing.

10
00:00:55.358 --> 00:01:03.217
Depending on the stop, proof can include a photo, signature, recipient name, note, and time or location context.

11
00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:11.075
Make sure the image is clear, the recipient information is correct, and the proof is shown as saved before leaving the customer.

12
00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:17.444
If the stop cannot be completed, use the exception path.

13
00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:23.813
Choose the reason that describes what happened, add a useful note, and preserve customer impact.

14
00:01:23.813 --> 00:01:30.181
Do not silently skip the stop.

15
00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:36.550
Message Dispatch whenever the exception changes route timing, stop order, customer expectations, safety, access, or the ability to complete later work.

16
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:44.933
After the stop is resolved, record departure and continue to the next stop.

17
00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:53.317
Finish the route only after every stop is completed, failed with a recorded reason, rescheduled, or otherwise resolved.

18
00:01:53.317 --> 00:02:01.700
A clean route history lets Dispatch, support, and the customer Champion understand what happened without rebuilding the day from text messages.

19
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:07.135
Protect delivery data throughout the route.

20
00:02:07.135 --> 00:02:12.570
Do not share sessions, access codes, proof images, customer details, or tracking links outside approved operational channels.

21
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:18.005
When support is needed, provide the route or stop identifier, the visible request ID, what you expected, and what happened.

22
00:02:18.005 --> 00:02:23.440
Never include a password or token.

23
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.875
Complete the quick check now.

24
00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:36.156
Now perform the practice task on the same device the Driver expects to use.

25
00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:43.438
Open the route, review a stop, record arrival, capture sanitized practice proof, send a message or exception, and record departure.

26
00:02:43.438 --> 00:02:50.719
Confirm that Dispatch can see each state change.

27
00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:58.000
If a permission, camera, network, or proof problem appears, resolve it before production and record the answer in the customer team notes.
